{
  "_comment": [
    "Generated from an actual probe run over fixtures/ and then reviewed by hand.",
    "After changing the fixtures or the codec set, re-derive it the same way:",
    "probe every fixture, and require the fields that are present today.",
    "must be present and non-empty. 'at least one fixture has it' would pass exactly",
    "the regression this gate exists to catch.",
    "requiredFields is the baseline; a fixture's own 'require' block replaces the",
    "baseline for that scope, and exists only where the codec genuinely cannot carry",
    "the field (theora and wmv2 report no profile; vp9, theora, wmv2 report no level;",
    "container-level bit rates are absent in matroska and mpegts).",
    "extradata_size is required on every fixture whose video streams carry it: it is the only field here that vanishes when the extract_extradata bitstream filter is absent, which is otherwise a completely silent failure (libavformat/demux.c skips the missing filter with no log line)."
  ],
  "emptyValues": [
    "",
    "0",
    "N/A",
    "unknown",
    "0/0",
    "-99"
  ],
  "requiredFields": {
    "format": [
      "format_name",
      "size",
      "nb_streams",
      "duration",
      "bit_rate"
    ],
    "video": [
